// Adversarial: Overcharge hazard active at 3 stacks against a Dense layout with chaos
// input, driving the per_kill_multiplier^kill_count compounding formula to its extremes.
//
// overcharge_count_kills tracks kills per bolt since the last bump. On a Dense board,
// a Bolt can destroy many cells in a single sweep before the player bumps — the speed
// multiplier is per_kill_multiplier^kill_count where per_kill_multiplier at 3 stacks
// is 1.0 + 0.05 + 2*0.03 = 1.11. After 30 kills without a bump the multiplier is
// 1.11^30 ≈ 22.9x, far above BoltMaxSpeed. The speed clamp must hold this value.
//
// Adversarial conditions:
//   - Dense layout: maximises cells-per-sweep before the next bump arrives, driving
//     kill_count high and exercising powi(kills) on large exponents
//   - 3 stacks: per_level_frac scaling beyond stack 1; non-trivial multiplier > 1.0
//   - Chaos input (0.5): moderate chaos ensures some bumps (resetting kill_count to 0)
//     interleaved with chaos-miss periods (allowing kill_count to climb)
//   - BoltSpeedAccurate: primary detector — compounding above BoltMaxSpeed is the failure
//   - NoNaN: powi on large integers can produce inf if multiplier is slightly off
//   - RunStatsMonotonic: cells_destroyed must not roll back when kill_count is reset by bump
//
// Edge case: overcharge_reset_on_bump runs after overcharge_count_kills in the same chain;
// if the ordering breaks, kills from the current tick could be reset before apply_speed
// sees them, or double-applied on the next tick.
(
    breaker: "Aegis",
    layout: "Dense",
    input: Chaos((action_prob: 0.5)),
    max_frames: 6000,
    disallowed_failures: [BoltInBounds, BoltSpeedAccurate, BreakerCountReasonable, BreakerInBounds, NoEntityLeaks, NoNaN, RunStatsMonotonic],
    allowed_failures: None,
    debug_setup: None,
    allow_early_end: false,
    seed: 3377,
    frame_mutations: [
        (frame: 30, mutation: InjectHazardStack(kind_name: "Overcharge", stacks: 3)),
    ],
)
